The  driver provides support for SBP‐2 devices that attach to the
IEEE1394 port.  It should work with all SBP‐2 devices  which  the
layer  supports, for example, HDDs, CDROM drives, and DVD drives.
Some users familiar with might wonder why the device is  not  de‐
tached at the layer when the device is unplugged.  It is detached
only  if the device has not been plugged again during several bus
resets.  This is for preventing to detach an active  file  system
even  when  the device cannot be probed correctly for some reason
after a bus reset or when the device  is  temporary  disconnected
because  the user changes the bus topology.  If you want to force
to detach the device, run several times.  The driver was  written
